1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:02,858
Meet MXI RoboICL.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,575
Our team builds on learning through context, with geometry

3
00:00:06,575 --> 00:00:08,757
that helps robots act more precisely.

4
00:00:10,598 --> 00:00:12,455
Start with one demonstration.

5
00:00:13,198 --> 00:00:16,435
Short windows, sampled across time, show the model how the

6
00:00:16,435 --> 00:00:17,643
task unfolds.

7
00:00:18,386 --> 00:00:21,993
Each window connects what the robot sees, the actions taken,

8
00:00:22,110 --> 00:00:23,506
and what happens next.

9
00:00:24,248 --> 00:00:26,731
The current episode follows the same format.

10
00:00:27,473 --> 00:00:30,448
Selected earlier interactions and the latest result join the

11
00:00:30,448 --> 00:00:32,530
demonstration in the model’s context.

12
00:00:33,273 --> 00:00:36,156
The model decides, acts, and observes again.

13
00:00:36,898 --> 00:00:38,480
Its weights stay frozen.

14
00:00:39,223 --> 00:00:41,430
Experience changes the conversation.

15
00:00:44,598 --> 00:00:46,306
The robot sees the object.

16
00:00:47,048 --> 00:00:48,818
But where will its fingers close?

17
00:00:49,561 --> 00:00:52,268
Our wrist guides make that closing center visible.

18
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:56,556
The camera is already there; we add projected gripper geometry.

19
00:00:57,298 --> 00:00:59,406
Watch the offset as the hand approaches.

20
00:01:00,148 --> 00:01:02,168
The target moves toward the crosshair.

21
00:01:02,911 --> 00:01:05,143
Align, close, and lift.

22
00:01:05,886 --> 00:01:09,011
The guide explains the alignment; the moving object reveals

23
00:01:09,011 --> 00:01:09,756
the result.

24
00:01:11,614 --> 00:01:14,596
A pixel tells us a direction, but not a distance.

25
00:01:15,339 --> 00:01:19,196
Now match the same vase opening in two calibrated camera views.

26
00:01:19,939 --> 00:01:21,909
Each observation defines a ray.

27
00:01:22,652 --> 00:01:25,876
Together, they constrain a three dimensional position, without

28
00:01:25,876 --> 00:01:26,784
a depth map.

29
00:01:27,526 --> 00:01:30,446
Here, the reconstructed depth is about half a metre.

30
00:01:31,189 --> 00:01:34,047
The third view is occluded, so it is excluded.

31
00:01:34,789 --> 00:01:38,552
Back in the recorded rollout, the robot uses geometric information

32
00:01:38,552 --> 00:01:39,896
while adjusting the pour.

33
00:01:41,750 --> 00:01:43,432
A target is only the beginning.

34
00:01:44,175 --> 00:01:46,557
The arm still needs a route it can execute.

35
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:50,658
Here, the first preview fails inverse kinematics.

36
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:52,732
No motion is sent.

37
00:01:53,475 --> 00:01:55,258
A revised plan passes.

38
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,158
Now watch a translucent preview of the recorded arm motion:

39
00:01:59,212 --> 00:02:02,932
approach, grasp, lift, transfer, and pour.

40
00:02:03,675 --> 00:02:05,745
Joint targets change along the route.

41
00:02:06,487 --> 00:02:10,125
This preview explains the accepted sequence; it is not a second

42
00:02:10,125 --> 00:02:11,282
physical robot.

43
00:02:12,025 --> 00:02:15,520
The overlay clears, and the recorded arm completes the task.

44
00:02:16,262 --> 00:02:18,258
The episode scores one hundred.

45
00:02:20,118 --> 00:02:23,450
MXI RoboICL keeps a compact foundation.

46
00:02:24,193 --> 00:02:27,663
The audited interface contains about six thousand characters.

47
00:02:28,405 --> 00:02:32,205
Across three exploratory task groups, our system loses fewer

48
00:02:32,205 --> 00:02:36,013
points than Q0 when readable task information is removed.

49
00:02:36,755 --> 00:02:40,143
Our updated system reaches seventy-five point nine in team

50
00:02:40,143 --> 00:02:41,388
self-evaluation.

51
00:02:42,130 --> 00:02:45,850
These results motivate a simple direction: learn from experience,

52
00:02:45,905 --> 00:02:49,638
make geometry explicit, and check motion before execution.

53
00:03:14,835 --> 00:03:16,780
MXI RoboICL.

54
00:03:17,523 --> 00:03:19,393
An MXI team upgrade.

55
00:03:20,135 --> 00:03:21,343
Thank you for watching.
